Editing this file runs the "Verify Maplerad proxy" workflow.

Why this exists: GitHub only shows the "Run workflow" button for workflows
that live on the repository's DEFAULT branch. This workflow is on a feature
branch, so there is no button until that merges. Changing this file is the
trigger instead — it is a path nothing else in the repo touches, so ordinary
work cannot fire it by accident. Each run calls a third party, which is why
that matters.

To run it from a phone: open this file on GitHub, tap the pencil, change the
line below to anything else, and commit. Then open Actions and read the run
summary.

Once the workflow reaches the default branch, use the button instead and
delete both this file and the `push` trigger in the workflow.

